{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ksuj6oyuvcbq534zpqco4l54qpqkvh3dzbh3od2g3ajabgkjx7qa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. Here's the summary.\n\n## What I found and did\n\n**The critical gap (Phase A):** `nm -D` on the C `.so` shows **28** exported symbols; the Rust crate exported **0** of them — it was a `[[bin]]`-only crate with no `crate-type`, no `#[no_mangle]`, and an internal representation that *cannot* be exported (`Vec<u8>` names, `&'static str` art rows, shape *indices* instead of `shape_t *`, a synthesised `%p` value). Per the Phase A rule I translated the missing C ABI surface rather than stubbing it: `src/capi/{shape,scene,app}.rs` mirrors `shape.c`, `scene.c` and `main.c` statement by statement — same `#[repr(C)]` layouts (verified against the C compiler: `sizeof(shape_t)=2444`, `sizeof(scene_t)=472`, all field offsets), same `malloc`/`free` singleton pattern (uninitialised `art` rows included), same libc stdio calls so `%p`, stream buffering and `scanf` push-back match by construction. `main.c` is part of the shared object, so all 13 app-level functions **and `main`** are exported too.\n\n**Artifacts** (all rows `[x]`): `SYMBOLS.md` (28/28 symbols, why the module was missing), `ERRORS.md` (81 rejection rows), `CONFIGS.md` (56 configuration rows, 10 axes).\n\n**Tests** — everything goes through `dlopen`/`dlsym` on both `.so`s, never a direct Rust call:\n| test | cases |\n|---|---|\n| `configs_lib` | 34 (rows 1‑30, 53‑56; randomised rows run 32‑64 inputs, seed `0x5EED2026`) |\n| `configs_app` | 218 (rows 31‑52, child process per scenario) |\n| `errors_lib` | 25 (rows 1‑38, 72‑81) |\n| `errors_app` | 126 (rows 1, 10, 39‑78) |\n| `binary_diff` | 179 executable scenarios (also covers the *idiomatic* translation) |\n| `symbols` | `nm -D` parity both directions + struct layout |\n\nNotable coverage: the allocator-failure branches are genuinely executed via an `LD_PRELOAD` size-selective `malloc` interposer (`tests/support/failmalloc.c`); the C code's infinite `while(getchar()!='\\n')` and its NULL-deref in `compare_shapes` are compared including killing signal and flushed-prefix bytes (which also validates the 4096-byte stdio buffering); printed `%p` values are normalised through the *same* id map as the struct dumps, so a consistently-wrong pointer can't hide.\n\n**Validation of the harness itself:** I mutated the Rust (`width 21→22`, a `printf` format, `\"Scene deleted\"`, in both the capi and the idiomatic code) and confirmed each mutation is caught; I also found and fixed a real test-validity trap — `cargo test` never rebuilds a `cdylib` no test links against, so tests now build the library via a nested `cargo build --lib` into a separate target dir.\n\n**Phase D:** symbol diff empty (28/28, no extras, only libc/libgcc undefined). Feature matrix: `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` and `c_src` has no `option()`/`#ifdef`, so `./check_all_features.sh` runs the 3 equivalent invocations (default / `--no-default-features` / `--all-features`) × check/build/test — all green.\n\nOnly `Cargo.toml` was modified (lib target, `libc`, `libloading` dev-dep); `c_src/` and the pre-existing `src/{main,cio,scene,shape}.rs` are untouched, and `dev_tests/compare.py` (51/51) and `fuzz.py` (90/90) still pass."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1305,"cache_read_input_tokens":353191,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1305,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a5152e0-686b-4b1f-b4ba-e422e6bc8db0","uuid":"64eba52d-94b0-470d-ac6e-75e3a63845e5","timestamp":"2026-08-19T23:58:41.134Z"}
